[04:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that animation starting for frame, use it as a reference, and then you can describe what sort of animation that you want, stepping forward, making a block attack, making a punch, whatever the case may be. Then, what we do is we send'

[04:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this video over to Auto Sprite and process all of those frames. And then we use the corridor key system on our local GPU to process all of those sprites. You can also use a cloud GPU.'

[05:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This process will nicely clean your green screen, and from here, we can send this over to Sprite Analyzer. From Sprite Analyzer, we can determine which of the frames we want to actually save'

